    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30169" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŭtĭna</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Cisalpine Gaul</i>, now <i>Modena</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				2, 4, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 5, 9, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 2,
			3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 5, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21,
			25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">35, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">41,
			20</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŭtĭnensis</span></b> , e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Mutina</i>: proelium, <i>near Mutina, between Antony
				and Octavius</i>, 711 A. U. C., <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 14, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4, 627</span></i>.</div>
